7. Checkpoint Types

Checkpoint| Meaning
"base.pt"| Starting checkpoint of the training run
"best.pt"| Best checkpoint based on validation loss
"live.pt"| Latest checkpoint that can continue training
"history/"| Old checkpoints kept as backups

Lower validation loss = better checkpoint.

---

8. Checkpoint Structure

checkpoints/
│
├── ored_v2/
│   ├── base.pt
│   ├── best.pt
│   └── live.pt
│
└── history/

Meaning

base.pt   = starting checkpoint
best.pt   = best validation checkpoint
live.pt   = latest resumable checkpoint
history/  = old checkpoint backups

