37. Add Training Data

Easiest: Supabase → Table Editor → ored_training_data → Insert → Insert row

Fill in:

type        qna
category    science
subject     physics
topic       mechanics
input       What is force?
output      Force is a push or pull that can change the motion of an object.
difficulty  beginner
language    en
dataset_tag facts           (or your own tag, or leave empty)
verified    true            (only verified rows are trained on)
enabled     true

Leave id, fingerprint, created_at and updated_at EMPTY. Supabase fills them.

Allowed "type": qna, fact, definition, vocabulary, sentence, conversation,
instruction, comprehension, correction, translation, math, reasoning,
writing, classification

Allowed "category": language_foundation, grammar, sentences, general_knowledge,
qna, conversation, mathematics, science, computer_science, engineering,
reasoning, instructions, reading, writing, language_skills, data, everyday,
safety, ored

See every type, category and usual subject:

RUN

python scripts\training_data.py taxonomy

Or add one row from the Command Prompt:

RUN

python scripts\training_data.py add --type qna --category science --subject physics --input "What is force?" --output "A push or a pull." --tag facts --verified

The same question with the same answer twice is refused:

DUPLICATE: 1 record(s) already exist with the same content ...

Edit the old row instead of adding a copy.
To stop using a row: set enabled = false. Do not delete it.

If you change facts.yaml, bring the changes to Supabase:

RUN

python scripts\training_data.py import-facts --skip-duplicates

