43. Supabase Data on Many PCs

Every PC must train on exactly the same data. So first take ONE snapshot
and save it to Supabase (on PC 1, after step 35):

RUN

python scripts\training_data.py snapshot --dataset-tag facts --upload

OUTPUT (end)

Train on exactly this snapshot:
  python scripts\train.py ... --snapshot 8466d709a23e1131...(64 letters)

Copy the 64-letter hash. Then do step 26 on EVERY PC, adding these three --set:

--set data.source=supabase --set data.supabase.dataset_tag=facts --set data.supabase.snapshot=PASTE_THE_64_LETTER_HASH

Example:

python scripts\distributed.py launch train --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --session ored_facts-run1 --rendezvous static --set run_name=ored_facts --set training.epochs=40 --set data.source=supabase --set data.supabase.dataset_tag=facts --set data.supabase.snapshot=PASTE_THE_64_LETTER_HASH -- --upload --report

Every PC downloads the same snapshot and checks it.
Without the hash it stops and tells you to take a snapshot first.

